<p>San Antonio hail damage claims are among the most common property insurance claims in Bexar County, and the weather record explains why. The NOAA Storm Events Database lists 618 hail reports in the county since 1957, and 203 of them were golf-ball size (1.75 inches) or larger. Reports cluster from March through May, with April the busiest month by a wide margin. The largest stone on record, 5.5 inches, fell near Sayers and the China Grove area on the east side on May 3, 2021 (<a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=961040" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NCEI event record</a>).</p>
<p>Hail damage is often harder to see than it sounds. Bruised shingles, cracked tiles, and dented metal can be invisible from the yard, and the full scope may show up only during a close roof inspection. This page explains what a hail claim usually involves, where disputes start, and how a public adjuster in San Antonio may help. For the numbers behind hail season, read <a href="/san-antonio-hail-season-storm-data/">San Antonio hail season storm data</a>.</p>

